WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.768
-Lenny, oh!

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.869
-What's happening, man?
What's happening?

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.902
Good to see you.

00:00:03.902 --> 00:00:05.437
-You look good, buddy.

00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:07.574
-You look great.
-Thank you, pal.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.309
Before we get into the book,

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:13.413
which I love,
I have a thousand questions.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:17.650
Halloween is almost upon us
and I've already --

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.153
we've already gotten pictures
that people sent

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:23.389
of kids dressing up
as you for Halloween.

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.324
It's a very popular costume.
Do you know that?

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.892
-I've seen it.
I've seen it.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:28.294
-This one here, though,
is my favorite.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.896
Look at this one.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.532
[ Laughter ].

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.202
-He got the plastic bag,
so he got it all.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.471
-He's got the bodega bag, yeah.
I just love it.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.340
I thought that was so funny
and so cute.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.876
I want to talk about your book,
"Let Love Rule."

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:46.579 line:0%
It documents the first
25 years of your life.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.348
You do some of the fun stories,

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.516
but also some
hard-hitting stories.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.652
Was it therapeutic for you
to write this?

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:58.391
-Extremely, and I found that,
while I was writing this book,

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.560
I was healed of so many
things in my past,

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.463
especially when it comes
to the relationship

00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:05.898
between myself and my father.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:11.071
We had a very -- we had a very
challenging relationship.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.605
Although we loved
each other very much,

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.940
but we, you know,
we had our challenges.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.611
And, in writing the book,
I was able to step back

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:23.482
and see people, and my father,
like characters.

00:01:23.482 --> 00:01:25.217
And I was able to really
have a clear look

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:28.120
at my father for the first time

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.989
and I saw him as a man
just trying to get

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:35.728
through this life experience
with what he had

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.097
and it was --
it was really healing

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:43.402
and I fell in love
with my father all over again

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.770
through writing this book.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.839
-You're very humble
in this book.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.741
Because, when you just look
at it, you go,

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.210
"Dude, it's Lenny Kravitz.
You're an icon."

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.181
You're a stud, you're talented,
you can play, you can write.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.983
But in this, you go like

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.518
you're growing up and you
have different phases

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.821
of singing
and who you want to be.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.557
But then you're like,
"Oh, I love Prince.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.826
I love David Bowie

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.028
-Mm-hmm.
-and, you know, Dylan."

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:13.433
And then, you end up touring
with a lot of these people.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:17.103
-Yeah. My very first tour
was Tom petty.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:20.706
He took me on an American
tour, playing arenas.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:23.142
And then, Bob Dylan
took me on tour.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.977
And then, David Bowie.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.713
Yeah, I opened for David Bowie
at Dodger Stadium.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.615
-Oh, my God.
-This is all during
my first album.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:32.251
It was magical.
-Wow!

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.852
What do you remember?
I mean, last time, I think,

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:36.389
you were on our show,
you brought a harmonica

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.957
that was Bob Dylan's harmonica

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.358
and you let me play it,
which was --

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:40.760
I'll never forget.
-That's right.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.428
That's right.
-I'll never forget it, buddy.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.798
What was Bob like when you
played with Bob Dylan?

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.967
-Bob was great, man, you know.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.802
He had an interest in me,
you know.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.070
We played at a festival together

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.907
somewhere in Europe
when we first met

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.508
and he kept telling people,

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.977
I want to meet
that Black Jewish kid."

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.379
-[ Laughs ]
-So he came --

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:02.281
Actually, I went
to his dressing room

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:05.852
and he invites me to go on this
tour and it was amazing and --

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.821
Except, one night,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:12.992
he called me to come out
to do "Maggie's Farm."

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.827
And he's like,
"Come out. Come out."

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.762
And I didn't know the words.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:18.397
Like, you know,
I know some of the words,

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:19.432
but I didn't know the words...

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.567
-Yeah.
-...so I kind of mumbled

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.802
-through it,
which I guess, kind of,

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.837
is the gig anyway, right?
So.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.639
-And it's Bob Dylan, so you
probably were going like,

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.073
"This is crazy.
I'm jamming with Bob

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:29.609
on 'Maggie's Farm.'"

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.410
That's the one he wanted you
out there for.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.880
-That's the one.
That's the one.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.283
-I love the book.
Again,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:41.654
who did you think
this book is for?

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.722
-I think, you know, the thing
that I've been hearing a lot of,

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:48.828
which I'm happy about is,

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:52.031
you know, it shows people that

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:56.069
you really have to find
your lane, your destiny,

00:03:56.069 --> 00:04:01.007
and to also stick to your dreams

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:05.344
and to your thought process
of how you think you should be.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:09.581
You know, I was offered so many
record deals and opportunities

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:12.117
and there were a lot
of open doors to me,

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:14.621
but, just because you have
open doors in your life

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:18.324
doesn't mean that you have
to walk through them, you know.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.660
Some are just to look into.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.897
-And, you know, for me,
it wasn't about money or fame.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.666
I turned down many deals,
as you --

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:30.736
as you can read in the book,
because they wanted to change

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.506
my vibe, my expression,
my whole thing,

00:04:34.506 --> 00:04:38.977
and I waited until
I actually found my sound

00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:43.115
and was able to, you know,
sign with a label

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:47.820
who was willing to allow me that
and to allow me to develop.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.755
-That must be so hard --
-So, you know, it's all about --

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.890
it's all about that journey
of finding your voice,

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.594
whatever that means,
in whatever field in your life.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.729 line:0%
-The book is called
"Let Love Rule."

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.030 line:0%
It's available now.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.031 line:0%
Everyone, pick it up.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:00.332 line:0%
It's fantastic.

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.000 line:0%
Lenny Kravitz,
we love you, buddy.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.636 line:0%
Come back whenever,
whenever, whenever.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.871 line:0%
Hopefully,
I get to see you in person.

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:07.373
-I love you, Jim.
Take care, man.
-I love you.

